<clickhouse>
    <!--
      Server memory ceiling.

      The stock ratio is 0.9, i.e. ~111 GiB of this host's 124 GiB. That is not a
      ceiling that protects anything: AGENTS.md records an unbounded full-history
      pass over raw_extrinsics/raw_events reaching ~84 GiB RSS, at which point the
      NEXT container to allocate tripped the kernel's global OOM killer, which took
      ClickHouse down and every service on the box with it. At 0.9 the server was
      still happily below its own limit the whole time.

      0.6 (~74 GiB) puts the ceiling BELOW that figure, so the same query is
      refused with MEMORY_LIMIT_EXCEEDED — a failed query and a stack trace instead
      of a dead host — and leaves ~50 GiB for the twenty-odd other containers that
      share this machine.

      This is a backstop, not a substitute for bounding a query. AGENTS.md still
      requires every ad-hoc pass over raw history to carry its own PREWHERE,
      max_memory_usage and max_threads, and to run in block-range chunks.
    -->
    <!--
      2026-10-09: 0.6 (~74 GiB) did not protect the host either. An unbounded join
      reached ~60 GiB, below the ceiling, while the node (35 GiB) and the rest of the
      box needed the remainder: the host swapped dry, stalled six minutes, and the
      global OOM killer took ClickHouse. Normal resident memory is 8-16 GiB, so the
      server is now capped at an absolute 40 GiB, and every query at 20 GiB
      (users.d/profile-limits.xml).

      The ratio goes back to 0.9 on purpose: the container now runs under a 48 GiB
      cgroup limit (docker-compose.yml mem_limit), and ClickHouse applies the ratio
      to the cgroup limit, not to the host's RAM. 0.6 of 48 GiB would silently pull
      the server down to ~29 GiB; 0.9 of 48 GiB (43 GiB) leaves 40 GiB the binding
      value whether or not the cgroup limit is set. 8 GiB between 40 and 48 covers
      what the server's tracker does not count, so the cgroup OOM (which kills only
      ClickHouse, never the host) is the last resort, not the first.
    -->
    <max_server_memory_usage>42949672960</max_server_memory_usage>
    <max_server_memory_usage_to_ram_ratio>0.9</max_server_memory_usage_to_ram_ratio>
</clickhouse>
